  <section class="hcm-ok-section hcm-ok-alt" id="features">
    <div class="hcm-ok-wrap">
      <div class="hcm-ok-hd center">
        <span class="hcm-ok-eyebrow">Feature Chapters</span>
        <h2>4D Massage Technology, Zero Gravity, and Body Scanning Compared</h2>
        <p>Each chapter answers one buyer question. Use them to narrow your Osaki vs Kyota comparison before a showroom visit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hcm-ok-feature-grid">
        <article class="hcm-ok-feature"><span class="hcm-ok-feature-label">Massage feel</span><h3>Which brand feels better?</h3><p>Osaki often gives buyers more choice across massage mechanisms and intensity styles. Kyota often feels easier to narrow because the lineup is more focused. The real answer depends on body type, pressure preference, and where you hold everyday tension. During a showroom visit, test both at your preferred intensity level and notice how each brand handles shoulder, mid-back, and lumbar zones differently.</p></article>
        <article class="hcm-ok-feature"><span class="hcm-ok-feature-label">4D / AI / Zero gravity</span><h3>Which brand has better 4D massage chair technology?</h3><p>Both brands offer strong 4D massage chair options. Osaki gives shoppers more 4D, 4D+, Duo, and AI configurations to compare across models like the <a href="{{ shop.url }}/products/osaki-op-ai-xrest-4d-plus-massage-chair" style="color:var(--gold)">Xrest 4D+</a> and <a href="{{ shop.url }}/products/osaki-grand-duo-4d-4d-massage-chair" style="color:var(--gold)">Grand Duo</a>. Kyota offers a cleaner premium 4D path through <a href="{{ shop.url }}/products/kyota-yugana-m780-4d-massage-chair" style="color:var(--gold)">Yugana M780</a>, <a href="{{ shop.url }}/products/kyota-hatsumei-m900-ai-4d-massage-chair" style="color:var(--gold)">Hatsumei M900 AI</a>, and <a href="{{ shop.url }}/products/kyota-nokori-m980-syner-d-massage-chair" style="color:var(--gold)">Nokori M980 Syner-D</a>. Zero gravity recline is available across both brands and should be tested in person to see how it changes pressure distribution on your body.</p></article>
        <article class="hcm-ok-feature"><span class="hcm-ok-feature-label">Back / neck / foot / calf</span><h3>Which Brand Is Better for Back, Neck, Foot, and Calf Comfort?</h3><p>For everyday tension, post-work recovery, and relaxation routines, test how the rollers land on your neck and shoulders, how mid-back pressure feels, and whether foot and calf massage is comfortable enough for repeated daily use. Kyota is often praised for strong lower-body and calf work. Osaki gives more mechanism variety that lets you compare different pressure styles. This is comfort guidance for daily wellness routines, not a medical claim.</p></article>
        <article class="hcm-ok-feature"><span class="hcm-ok-feature-label">Space and home fit</span><h3>Which brand fits the home better?</h3><p>Room size, recline clearance, wall distance, user height, and family preferences all matter. Some Osaki models include space-saving recline designs, but Duo models are larger by nature. Kyota's focused lineup can make room-planning simpler. Measure your intended room, check the reclined length and wall clearance for any model on your shortlist, and bring those measurements to a showroom consultation.</p></article>
        <article class="hcm-ok-feature"><span class="hcm-ok-feature-label">Family use</span><h3>Which brand suits a multi-user household?</h3><p>Osaki may suit households where different family members want different intensity levels, program variety, and feature depth. Kyota may suit households that want a simpler premium routine everyone can enjoy without programming complexity. Consider adjustable intensity settings, user memory profiles, and how easy the controls are for less tech-confident users. Test the controller during your showroom visit.</p></article>
        <article class="hcm-ok-feature"><span class="hcm-ok-feature-label">Price and value</span><h3>Price, Warranty, Delivery, and Long-Term Value</h3><p>Osaki has broader pricing and model coverage, from value-led entry points like <a href="{{ shop.url }}/products/osaki-oasis-massage-chair" style="color:var(--gold)">Oasis</a> and <a href="{{ shop.url }}/products/osaki-ziva-massage-chair" style="color:var(--gold)">Ziva</a> to flagship dual-engine systems. Kyota has a focused ladder from practical daily comfort through mid-tier 4D to flagship Syner-D. Final value depends on body fit, frequency of use, whether the buyer will actually use the features daily, and the warranty and support that comes with an authorized dealer purchase. Prices and availability may change — check product pages for current information.</p></article>
        <article class="hcm-ok-feature"><span class="hcm-ok-feature-label">Warranty and support</span><h3>Authorized Dealer Trust and Long-Term Ownership</h3><p>Both Osaki and Kyota massage chairs include manufacturer-backed warranties covering parts, labor, and frame when purchased from an authorized dealer like House of Massage Chairs. HOMC coordinates warranty claims on your behalf, provides white-glove delivery and setup when available, and offers expert post-purchase support. Buying from an authorized specialist ensures genuine products with valid warranties — unauthorized marketplace sellers may not honor warranty claims or provide professional installation.</p></article>
